:"2026-10-24T15:10:07.782Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-9p44mk9j/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/mlflow-operator.md","content":"# Component: mlflow-operator\n\n## Metadata\n\n- **Repository**: https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/mlflow-operator.git\n- **Version**: 8a8c12a2a3df1349b1bd5424c42f4214b8206d62\n- **Distribution**: RHOAI\n- **Languages**: Go\n- **Deployment Type**: Kubernetes Operator / Controller\n- **Generated By**: Claude Opus 4.6 on 2026-08-13\n\n## Purpose\n\n**Short**: Kubernetes operator that manages the lifecycle of MLflow Tracking Server instances on OpenShift, including Helm-based deployment, Gateway API routing, namespace-scoped workspace RBAC, and integration with the RHOAI platform Auth service. [source: cmd/main.go:171, internal/controller/mlflow_controller.go:539, internal/controller/namespace_rbac_controller.go:67]\n\n**Detailed**: mlflow-operator is a controller-runtime operator that reconciles three custom resources — `MLflow` (mlflow.opendatahub.io/v1), `MLflowOperator` (components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1), and `MLflowConfig` (mlflow.kubeflow.org/v1) — to deploy and manage MLflow Tracking Server instances on RHOAI. The MLflow controller renders Helm charts into Kubernetes resources (Deployments, Services, PersistentVolumeClaims, CronJobs, NetworkPolicies) and conditionally creates Gateway API HTTPRoutes, OpenShift ConsoleLinks, and Prometheus ServiceMonitors based on cluster capability discovery. A dedicated NamespaceRBACReconciler watches the platform Auth CRD (`services.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1`) and labeled namespaces to propagate view/edit RoleBindings for workspace-level access control. The operator uses leader election, caches filtered by label selectors, and field-selector-scoped watches for shared RBAC objects to minimize API server load. [source: cmd/main.go:171, 272, 300, internal/controller/mlflow_controller.go:473-552, internal/controller/namespace_rbac_controller.go:48-106, internal/controller/routing.go:46-179]\n\n## Architectural Analysis\n\nmlflow-operator follows a multi-controller architecture built on controller-runtime v0.23.3. The primary **MLflowReconciler** owns the full lifecycle of MLflow Tracking Server deployments: it renders bundled Helm charts into Kubernetes objects (Deployments, Services, Secrets, ServiceAccounts, PersistentVolumeClaims, CronJobs, and NetworkPolicies) and applies them via server-side apply with owner references. The controller conditionally extends its watch surface at startup using the Kubernetes discovery API — adding Gateway API HTTPRoute, OpenShift ConsoleLink, and Prometheus ServiceMonitor watches only when those CRDs are present in the cluster. This discovery-gated pattern avoids hard dependencies on optional platform APIs. [source: internal/controller/mlflow_controller.go:528-552, internal/controller/routing.go:46-179]\n\nThe **MLflowOperatorReconciler** manages the component-level `MLflowOperator` CRD from `components.platform.opendatahub.io`, acting as the integration surface for the RHOAI platform operator (odh-operator). A dedicated **NamespaceRBACReconciler** watches namespaces labeled with `opendatahub.io/mlflow-workspace`, the platform Auth CRD (`services.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1`), and MLflow CRs to propagate view/edit RoleBindings into workspace namespaces, enabling multi-tenant access isolation delegated through the platform's centralized auth configuration. [source: internal/controller/namespace_rbac_controller.go:48-106, internal/controller/mlflowoperator_controller.go:76-143]\n\nThe operator restricts its Kubernetes API footprint through label-selector-filtered caches (keyed on `app=mlflow`) and field-selector-scoped watches for shared RBAC objects (ClusterRole/ClusterRoleBinding filtered by `metadata.name`). Secret access is restricted via `resourceNames`-scoped RBAC to the single `mlflow-artifact-connection` secret per namespace. The metrics endpoint on port 8443 is protected by controller-runtime's TokenReview/SubjectAccessReview filter with TLS (self-signed or operator-provided certificates), while health and readiness probes on port 8081 are unauthenticated by design. FIPS compliance is enforced at build time via `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime` and dynamic linking against OpenSSL on UBI9. [source: cmd/main.go:267-284, 293-318, Dockerfile.konflux:31-32, config/rbac/role.yaml:2]\n\n## Provenance\n\n### Repo Lineage\n\n| Role | Repository | Sync Mechanism | Sync Branch | Sync Workflows | Detection Method |\n|----|----------|--------------|-----------|--------------|----------------|\n| Upstream | https://github.com/opendatahub-io/mlflow-operator | manual | main | -- | sync_config |\n| Downstream | https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/mlflow-operator | manual | main | -- | local_analysis |\n\n### Aliases\n\n| Current Name | Previous Name | Type | Context |\n|------------|-------------|----|-------|\n\n## Architecture Components\n\n| Component | Type | Purpose |\n|---------|----|-------|\n| Dockerfile.konflux:ENTRYPOINT | Container entrypoint | [\"/manager\"] |\n| Dockerfile:ENTRYPOINT | Container entrypoint | [\"/manager\"] |\n| MLflow controller | Controller | Reconciles MLflow resources |\n| MLflowOperator controller | Controller | Reconciles MLflowOperator resources |\n| Namespace controller | Controller | Reconciles Namespace resources |\n| cmd | Go controller-runtime operator | cmd |\n| mlflow-operator-controller-manager | Deployment | manager (controller:latest) |\n| mlflow-tests/images/Dockerfile.konflux:ENTRYPOINT | Container entrypoint | [\"bash\", \"mlflow-tests/images/test-run.sh\"] |\n\n## APIs Exposed\n\n### Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs)\n\nCRD count scope: 3 core API CRDs; 3 total CRD/API rows including configuration and visibility APIs.\n\n| Group | Version | Kind | Scope | API Role | Purpose |\n|-----|-------|-